## 1. Summary of Delivery

Commit 37c9cd2 introduces two stdlib-only fuzzers:
1. `tools/fuzz-fat32.py`: targets `tools/verify-fat32.py` against `kernel/src/fat32_corpus.img`. It builds an exact coverage set of 384 bytes in 391 deterministic probes derived from the EFI FAT32 specification and corpus provenance manifest `tools/fat32-corpus-manifest.json`, followed by 2,000 single-bit random mutations (70% exact pool, 30% uniform).
2. `tools/fuzz-package.py`: targets `tools/verify-manifest.py` and `tools/nova_trust.py`. It tests verification against OpenSSL fixture `tests/fixtures/ed25519-openssl.json`, package file tampering, manifest text mutations, deterministic adversarial documents, raw `nova_trust.verify` mutations, and PEM key formatting mutations.

Both fuzzers currently exit 1 due to genuine defect findings in the targets, which freebuff reported in `docs/logs/d3-findings.log` and properly left unfixed per AGENTS.md rules.

