## 4. Sensitivity Proven by Independent Planted Faults in Scratch Clone

In an independent scratch clone at `%TEMP%\d3-review-scratch`, two new planted faults (distinct from author's plants) were introduced in the targets to verify sensitivity.

### 4.1 Plant 1: Disable FSInfo Lead Signature Check in `tools/verify-fat32.py`
Neutralized `need(struct.unpack_from("<I", fsi, 0)[0] == 0x41615252, "FSInfo lead sig")`.
Running `py -3 tools/fuzz-fat32.py` against the mutant:
```
fuzz-fat32:   probe MISS FSInfo lead sig byte 0 @ byte 512: exit 0 (not detected)
fuzz-fat32:   probe MISS FSInfo lead sig byte 1 @ byte 513: exit 0 (not detected)
fuzz-fat32:   probe MISS FSInfo lead sig byte 2 @ byte 514: exit 0 (not detected)
fuzz-fat32:   probe MISS FSInfo lead sig byte 3 @ byte 515: exit 0 (not detected)
fuzz-fat32: probes: 369/391 single-byte structural mutations detected (4 false passes, 18 crashes)
fuzz-fat32: false pass: 629/2000 reported success, classified:
fuzz-fat32:           structural: 12  <- must be 0; >0 is a target defect  [e.g. byte 513: 0x52->0x42]
fuzz-fat32: structural false passes: 12
fuzz-fat32: FAIL
```
Movement: Probes detected dropped from 373 to 369 (4 false passes). Random structural false passes increased from 0 to 12.

### 4.2 Plant 2: Weaken Replay Protection Check in `tools/nova_trust.py`
Weakened `seq <= last_accepted_sequence` to `seq < last_accepted_sequence` in `verify_manifest`.
Running `py -3 tools/fuzz-package.py` against the mutant:
```
fuzz-package: probes (signature, replay, files): 4/5 mutations rejected, 1 false passes, 0 crashes
fuzz-package:   FALSE PASS replay: state equals release_sequence: exit 0, wanted reject (['verify-manifest: PASS'])
fuzz-package: crashes: 2
fuzz-package: false passes: 1
fuzz-package: FAIL
```
Movement: Probe rejection dropped from 5/5 to 4/5, detecting 1 false pass where replay of identical sequence number was accepted.

Both fuzzers demonstrate acute sensitivity to target omissions and regressions.

